{
  "_comment": "Parity test actors for the local/ephemeral compose stack only (compose/scripts/init-env.sh --parity-fixtures). Layered onto the identity repo's realm by the parity-fixtures-import service after realm-import; never imported anywhere else. Customer actors are members of /customers (the group the customer service's fine-grained admin permission covers); staff actors are not. init-env renders it into .cache/parity/ and adds the realm's LDAP federation as disabled (no OpenLDAP in compose). Client parity-tpp is a Keycloak-mode open-finance TPP (private_key_jwt, DPoP-bound, client credentials only): init-env generates its keypair at runtime (private JWK only in .env), the renderer adds the public JWKS and copies audiences and client scopes from the realm's of-tpp-conformance-template.",
  "realm": "fintechbankx",
  "users": [
    {
      "username": "parity-banker",
      "enabled": true,
      "emailVerified": true,
      "firstName": "Parity",
      "lastName": "Banker",
      "email": "parity-banker@parity.invalid",
      "realmRoles": [
        "banker"
      ],
      "credentials": [
        {
          "type": "password",
          "value": "$(env:PARITY_PASSWORD_BANKER)",
          "temporary": false
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "username": "parity-admin",
      "enabled": true,
      "emailVerified": true,
      "firstName": "Parity",
      "lastName": "Admin",
      "email": "parity-admin@parity.invalid",
      "realmRoles": [
        "admin"
      ],
      "credentials": [
        {
          "type": "password",
          "value": "$(env:PARITY_PASSWORD_ADMIN)",
          "temporary": false
        }
      ]
    },
    {
